- Summary:: The book "When Schools Work" by Bruce Fuller discusses how activists revived public schools in Los Angeles through new political alliances in the 1990s. A diverse group, including Black and Latino leaders and reform-minded educators, united to challenge the centralized control of schools. Their efforts led to the rise of charter schools and aimed to improve education for underserved communities.
